.TH LIUXIN 1 "2026-10-23" "LiuXin-alpha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
liuxin \- manage a LiuXin catalogue, storage and workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B liuxin
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B liuxin init
.I SYSTEM_ROOT
.br
.B liuxin
.I command
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
LiuXin provides named commands for catalogue operations, managed storage,
metadata and acquisition workflows.
Use
.B liuxin \-\-help
to list command families and a family's
.B \-\-help
to inspect its current subcommands.
.PP
For remote-file registration and optional downloads, see
.BR liuxin-ingest-web (1).
For the distinction between web and local-file ingest, see
.BR liuxin-ingest (1).
.SH SETUP
Run
.B liuxin init
in a terminal, or explicitly use
.BR "liuxin init \-\-wizard" .
Choose the database backend, system root, optional primary Store, and whether
to use the system by default for future commands. Saving the default is offered
with Yes selected. Confirm the displayed plan before initialization begins.
The default is saved after successful setup; declining keeps the old selection.
.PP
For noninteractive path-backed setup, use
.B liuxin init SYSTEM_ROOT \-\-make-default
to request the same persistence. A system manifest is required.
For an existing installation, use
.BR "liuxin connect SYSTEM_ROOT" .
Inspect the selection with
.B liuxin connect status
and forget it with
.BR "liuxin disconnect" .
Disconnect does not delete the catalogue or stored files.
.PP
Defaults belong to the current operating-system user and are saved in
XDG_CONFIG_HOME/liuxin/active-connection.json, normally
~/.config/liuxin/active-connection.json. The file contains a manifest pointer,
not copied credentials. Commands run through sudo normally use root's separate
configuration; supply an explicit system root when selecting another user's
installation. Setup reports environment selectors that override the new default.
.SH CONNECTION SELECTION
Core-backed commands accept one of
.BR \-\-system-root " " DIRECTORY ,
.BR \-\-profile " " PROFILE ,
.BR \-\-database " " PATH ,
or
.BR \-\-core-endpoint " " URL .
A saved connection from
.B liuxin connect
can supply the default. Explicit selectors take precedence over environment
selectors and saved connections.
.PP
.B \-\-core-token-file PATH
supplies a remote Core bearer token.
Remote web-ingest execution requires trusted Core authority.
Local filesystem paths used by managed workflows belong to the Core host;
CLI output files belong to the CLI host.
.SH OUTPUT
Operational commands return JSON. Use
.B \-\-compact
for compact JSON and
.B \-\-output PATH
for a CLI-host output file.
.B \-\-replace-output
permits replacement of an existing output file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
liuxin init "$HOME/LiuXin" \-\-make-default
liuxin storage status
liuxin storage status \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web https://example.org/books/ \e
  \-\-system-root "$HOME/LiuXin"
liuxin ingest web \-\-help
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIUXIN_SYSTEM_ROOT
Select a system root when no explicit selector is supplied.
.TP
.B LIUXIN_PROFILE
Select a configured profile.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Parent of LiuXin's profile and saved-connection configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR liuxin-ingest (1),
.BR liuxin-ingest-web (1)
.PP
The source checkout contains user guides in
.B docs/
and implementation documentation in
.BR dev-docs/ .
